SUMMARY:Best of Union Beats: Classic Roots
DESCRIPTION:We’re bringing our favourite DJs from our indoor Union Beats program to the patio. Turn up your midday with the best beats in the city. Union Summer’s mid-day DJ sessions bring laid-back vibes and feel-good energy to the patio—perfect for a break in the sun. Whether you’re grabbing a bite\, meeting friends\, or just soaking it all in\, our DJs are spinning the ultimate soundtrack to your day. \nJoshua “Classic Roots” DePerry is an Indigenous DJ\, music producer\, and performer of Ojibwe and Blackfoot heritage. Originally from Thunder Bay and Long Lake 58 First Nation and now based in Toronto\, he is recognized for blending electronic music with traditional Indigenous rhythms to create a sound that is both innovative and deeply rooted in culture. \nHis high-energy performances have appeared on national and international stages including Future Forest\, TIFF\, imagineNATIVE\, Luminato\, and London’s Trafalgar Square. Through music\, Classic Roots celebrates cultural pride\, resilience\, and creativity while delivering unforgettable dancefloor experiences.
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/best-of-union-beats-classic-roots/
LOCATION:Union\, 65 Front Street West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Union Summer
